# Paths under the job user's home kept on the remote's own disk instead of dev's, one
# per line. File locks do not work between dev and an NFS client, so a shared tool cache
# would corrupt. A path missing on dev is skipped. Kept per user and reused between jobs.
# `ro <path>` binds it read-only: what a job writes there would stay on the remote, never
# reach dev (a container image), so the write fails with EROFS instead.
.cache/go-build
go/pkg/mod
.cache/uv
.cache/pre-commit
ro .local/share/containers
ro .cache/containers
.cache/Microsoft
